# BRAND_GUIDELINES.md

# Attar Brand - Brand Guidelines

Version: 1.0

---

# Brand Vision

To become one of Bangladesh's most trusted premium attar brands by offering authentic, long-lasting, alcohol-free fragrances with a luxurious shopping experience.

---

# Brand Mission

Deliver premium-quality attars that combine elegance, tradition, and modern luxury while ensuring excellent customer service and affordable pricing.

---

# Brand Values

- Authenticity
- Premium Quality
- Trust
- Elegance
- Simplicity
- Long-lasting Fragrance
- Customer Satisfaction

---

# Brand Personality

Our brand should always feel:

- Elegant
- Luxury
- Minimal
- Modern
- Confident
- Sophisticated
- Premium
- Warm
- Trustworthy

Never feel:

- Cheap
- Noisy
- Colorful
- Cluttered
- Over-designed
- Aggressive

---

# Target Audience

Primary

- Men (18–45)
- Working Professionals
- Students
- Fragrance Enthusiasts

Secondary

- Women
- Gift Buyers
- Couples
- Premium Product Lovers

---

# Brand Promise

Premium fragrance in every drop.

We promise:

- Alcohol-Free Attar
- Long-lasting fragrance
- Premium imported fragrance oils
- Affordable luxury
- Reliable customer support
- Secure shopping experience

---

# Brand Positioning

We are not a discount perfume store.

We are a premium attar brand focused on quality, elegance, and customer experience.

Every interaction should reinforce luxury and trust.

---

# Tone of Voice

The writing should always be:

- Professional
- Friendly
- Premium
- Confident
- Simple
- Helpful

Avoid:

- Clickbait
- Spammy marketing
- Excessive emojis
- ALL CAPS
- Overly dramatic claims

---

# Writing Style

Use short, readable sentences.

Highlight product benefits before features.

Focus on experience instead of only specifications.

Good Example

"Fresh citrus notes with a clean woody finish—perfect for daily wear."

Bad Example

"BEST ATTAR EVER!!! BUY NOW!!!"

---

# Brand Taglines

Primary

Luxury in Every Drop

Alternative

The Essence of Elegance

Pure Attar. Pure Identity.

Crafted for Every Occasion.

Inspired by Tradition. Designed for Today.

Long-Lasting Luxury.

Choose one primary tagline and use others selectively.

---

# Visual Identity

The interface should communicate:

- Luxury
- Cleanliness
- Simplicity
- Premium craftsmanship

Whitespace is an important design element.

Never overcrowd the layout.

---

# Color Palette

Primary

Black
#0B0B0B

Secondary

Gold
#C8A96A

Background

White
#FFFFFF

Surface

#F7F7F7

Text Primary

#1E1E1E

Text Secondary

#666666

Border

#E5E5E5

Optional Accent

Emerald Green
#0F766E

Status Colors

Success
#16A34A

Warning
#F59E0B

Error
#DC2626

Avoid neon or overly saturated colors.

---

# Typography

Headings

Playfair Display

Alternative

Cormorant Garamond

Body

Inter

Alternative

Manrope

UI

Inter

Font hierarchy should clearly distinguish headings, body text, and UI labels.

---

# Buttons

Primary

Black background

White text

Hover → Gold accent

Secondary

White background

Black border

Hover → Light gray

Danger

Red

Only for destructive actions.

---

# Border Radius

Cards

16px

Buttons

12px

Inputs

12px

Images

16–20px

Maintain consistent rounded corners across the site.

---

# Shadows

Soft shadows only.

Avoid heavy shadows.

Example

Small shadow for cards

Medium shadow on hover

---

# Icons

Use a clean outline icon set.

Examples

- Lucide Icons
- Heroicons

Icons should remain simple and consistent.

---

# Photography Style

Use:

- High-resolution images
- Soft lighting
- Premium packaging
- Glass bottles
- Dark luxury backgrounds
- Gold accents
- Natural textures (wood, marble, fabric)

Avoid:

- Low-quality images
- Busy backgrounds
- Mixed lighting
- Watermarks

---

# Product Images

Preferred ratio

1:1

Minimum width

1200px

Transparent background preferred for catalog images.

Lifestyle images may use decorative backgrounds.

---

# Banner Style

Large imagery

Elegant typography

Minimal text

One clear call-to-action

Examples

Experience the Essence of Pure Attar

Luxury Fragrance Collection

Premium Alcohol-Free Attars

---

# Product Card Style

Display

- Image
- Product Name
- Price
- Size Options
- Stock Badge
- Wishlist Button
- Quick Add

Hover

- Slight elevation
- Soft zoom
- Shadow increase

---

# Badge Style

Examples

Best Seller

New Arrival

Limited Edition

Premium

Exclusive

Out of Stock

Badges should be subtle and elegant.

---

# Animations

Allowed

Fade

Slide

Scale

Hover lift

Duration

150–300ms

Avoid flashy or distracting animations.

---

# User Experience Principles

Prioritize:

- Simplicity
- Speed
- Readability
- Accessibility
- Mobile-first design

Users should find any product within three clicks or fewer.

---

# Trust Elements

Highlight throughout the website:

- Alcohol-Free
- Premium Imported Oils
- Long Lasting
- Authentic Products
- Fast Delivery
- Secure Payment
- Customer Support

---

# Customer Experience

Every page should answer:

Why trust this brand?

Why buy this fragrance?

Why buy today?

Reduce friction during shopping.

---

# Content Guidelines

Product descriptions should include:

- Fragrance profile
- Ideal season
- Best occasion
- Longevity
- Suitable audience

Avoid exaggerated or unverifiable claims.

---

# SEO Guidelines

Every page should include:

- Unique title
- Meta description
- Open Graph image
- Structured data where applicable

URLs should remain short and readable.

Example

/products/blue-mask

instead of

/products/product-12345

---

# Accessibility

Support:

- Keyboard navigation
- Visible focus states
- High color contrast
- Descriptive alt text
- Semantic HTML

Meet WCAG AA guidelines where practical.

---

# Future Branding Assets

The design should accommodate future additions such as:

- Brand logo updates
- Seasonal campaigns
- Gift packaging
- Loyalty program
- Membership tiers
- Mobile app branding

---

# Consistency Rules

All pages must use:

- The same spacing system
- The same typography scale
- The same color palette
- The same button styles
- The same card components
- The same icon style
- The same animation language

Consistency takes priority over novelty.

---

# Integration Notes

This document defines the brand identity only.

Business information belongs in:

- PRODUCT_CATALOG.md
- BUSINESS_REQUIREMENTS.md

UI implementation belongs in:

- REDESIGN_PLAN.md

Claude CLI should follow this file to maintain a consistent premium brand experience across every page and component.
</file>

<file path="docs/BUSINESS_REQUIREMENTS.md">
# BUSINESS_REQUIREMENTS.md

> **Document Purpose**
>
> This document defines the business goals, user expectations, required website functionality, and future roadmap for the KAHF Treasure website.
>
> It does not describe implementation details or UI components.
>
> All design and development decisions should support these business requirements.

---

# Project Information

## Business Name

KAHF Treasure

## Business Type

Premium Alcohol-Free Attar & Islamic Lifestyle Brand

## Industry

Fragrance / Attar / Islamic Lifestyle Products

## Primary Market

Bangladesh

## Business Model

Direct-to-Customer (D2C)

Customers browse products online and place orders primarily through WhatsApp, Facebook Messenger, or direct contact.

Currently there is **no online payment gateway** and **no checkout system**.

---

# Business Goals

The website should help the business achieve the following goals.

## Primary Goals

- Build trust with new customers.
- Present KAHF Treasure as a premium brand.
- Increase WhatsApp orders.
- Make browsing products simple.
- Increase customer engagement.
- Improve conversion rate.
- Strengthen online brand presence.

---

## Secondary Goals

- Improve search engine visibility (SEO).
- Encourage repeat customers.
- Make future expansion easier.
- Support future e-commerce functionality.
- Reduce customer confusion during ordering.

---

# Target Audience

The website is primarily designed for:

- Customers in Bangladesh.
- People interested in premium alcohol-free attar.
- Islamic lifestyle customers.
- Gift buyers.
- Customers looking for long-lasting fragrances.
- Mobile-first users.
- Social-media-driven shoppers.

---

# Brand Position

The business should be perceived as:

- Premium
- Elegant
- Authentic
- Trustworthy
- Islamic
- Modern
- Customer Friendly

The website should create confidence before asking customers to place an order.

---

# Website Objectives

The website should:

- Showcase products professionally.
- Explain the brand story.
- Build customer trust.
- Make product discovery easy.
- Help customers choose the right fragrance.
- Encourage customers to contact the business.
- Increase WhatsApp conversations.
- Support future online shopping features.

---

# Customer Journey

A visitor should naturally move through this flow.

1. Discover the brand.
2. Understand why KAHF Treasure is different.
3. Browse collections.
4. Explore products.
5. Compare options.
6. Build confidence.
7. Contact the business.
8. Place an order.

Every page should reduce friction during this journey.

---

# Required Website Sections

The homepage should include:

- Hero Section
- Brand Story
- Why Choose Us
- Featured Products
- Most Wanted Collection
- New Arrivals
- Oud Collection
- Floral Collection
- Fruit Collection
- Premium Packages
- Customer Reviews
- Frequently Asked Questions
- Contact Section
- Footer

---

# Required Business Features

The website should support:

- Product browsing
- Category browsing
- Collection browsing
- Product search
- Featured products
- Best sellers
- New arrivals
- Stock status
- WhatsApp ordering
- Facebook contact
- Email contact
- Mobile-friendly experience
- Responsive design
- SEO optimization

---

# Product Information Requirements

Every product should eventually support:

- Product Name
- Product Image
- Category
- Short Description
- Price
- Available Sizes
- Fragrance Family
- Fragrance Notes
- Longevity
- Projection
- Recommended Season
- Recommended Occasion
- Gender
- Availability
- Featured Badge
- New Arrival Badge
- Best Seller Badge

Not every product currently contains all of these fields, but the system should be designed to support them in the future.

---

# Trust Building Requirements

The website should communicate:

- Alcohol-Free Products
- Premium Imported Oils
- Long Lasting Fragrance
- Authentic Quality
- Fast Delivery
- Customer Satisfaction
- Secure Ordering Process

Future additions may include:

- Customer testimonials
- Ratings
- Reviews
- Delivery information
- Return policy
- Privacy policy
- Shipping policy

---

# Conversion Requirements

The website should encourage visitors to:

- Browse products.
- Compare fragrances.
- Discover collections.
- Contact through WhatsApp.
- Request recommendations.
- Purchase premium packages.

Every major section should include a clear call-to-action.

---

# Contact Requirements

The website should provide:

- WhatsApp
- Facebook
- Email
- Phone Number
- Business Address (if available)
- Google Maps (future)

Customers should always have an easy way to contact the business.

---

# Content Requirements

The website should contain:

- Brand Story
- Mission
- Vision
- Product Information
- Fragrance Guides
- Frequently Asked Questions
- Ordering Instructions

Future content may include:

- Blog Articles
- Fragrance Education
- Buying Guides
- Seasonal Recommendations

---

# Search Engine Optimization

The website should be optimized for search engines.

Goals include:

- Fast loading speed.
- Mobile optimization.
- Structured metadata.
- Semantic HTML.
- Open Graph support.
- Product schema.
- Organization schema.
- Sitemap.
- Robots configuration.

---

# Accessibility Requirements

The website should be usable for all visitors.

Requirements include:

- Keyboard navigation.
- Proper color contrast.
- Readable typography.
- Screen reader support.
- Reduced motion support.
- Mobile accessibility.

---

# Performance Requirements

The website should prioritize:

- Fast loading.
- Optimized images.
- Minimal JavaScript.
- Good Core Web Vitals.
- Efficient rendering.
- Lightweight components.

---

# Future Business Features

These features are planned but not required for the first release.

## Shopping

- Shopping Cart
- Checkout
- Online Payment
- Cash on Delivery
- Order Tracking

---

## Customer Features

- Wishlist
- Compare Products
- Recently Viewed
- Loyalty Program
- Referral Program
- Coupon System
- Gift Cards

---

## Marketing

- Newsletter Subscription
- Promotional Campaigns
- Discount Banners
- Seasonal Offers

---

## Product Experience

- Product Reviews
- Product Ratings
- Related Products
- Fragrance Finder Quiz
- Personalized Recommendations

---

## Business Management

- Inventory Management
- Admin Dashboard
- Product Management
- Analytics Dashboard

---

# Success Metrics

The redesign should improve:

- WhatsApp inquiries
- Customer trust
- Time spent on the website
- Product discovery
- Mobile experience
- Search engine visibility
- Customer engagement
- Brand perception
- Conversion rate

---

# Business Constraints

The redesign must:

- Preserve all existing product information.
- Preserve existing contact channels.
- Maintain a premium brand identity.
- Remain fast and responsive.
- Be easy to maintain.
- Support future business growth.
- Allow future e-commerce expansion without major redesign.

---

# Final Business Vision

KAHF Treasure should be recognized as one of Bangladesh's most trusted premium alcohol-free attar brands.

The website should not feel like a simple product catalog. It should represent a complete luxury fragrance brand that builds trust, creates desire, and encourages customers to place orders while remaining scalable for future business growth.
</file>

